#X obj 654 11 risset.gliss;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 276 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 the object calculates the MIDI pitches and amplitudes
for a Sheppard–Risset glissando: an auditory illusion of a tone that
seems to rise or fall endlessly without ever reaching a limit;
#X text 240 153 the illusion is created by several frequency components
spaced an octave apart. Each component is shifted in frequency \, while
its amplitude follows a bell-shaped envelope that peaks near the center
of the audible range. When a component reaches the edge of the range
\, it fades out and a new component fades in at the opposite edge \,
so the listener perceives continuous motion;
#X text 240 269 the input value is the glissando phase \, typically
driven by a ramp from 0 to 1\. The first outlet outputs a list of MIDI
pitches \, the second outlet outputs the corresponding list of amplitudes;
#X msg 69 402 1 \, 0 10000;
#X msg 50 431 0 \, 1 10000;
